+    //
+    // ear: sendspin-listener.patch. If the inbound slots are full, an occupant that has proved
+    // nothing gives way, or two silent sockets, renewed before the establish reap, would keep every
+    // server out. What decides is what cannot be had for nothing: an occupant from the newcomer's
+    // own address goes first, so one address, however fast, touches no other's; then one with its
+    // Noise handshake unfinished; then, of those, the oldest. Finished with the Sentinel or Pairing
+    // PSK it has proved nothing either (anyone holds the first, and the second is checked only
+    // after this point), so it goes only when no weaker one is there. Only a long-term PSK proves a
+    // server: its first Noise message needs that server's private key, so it, and an operational
+    // entry about to be admitted, never gives way, and
+    // the newcomer is rejected only when those fill the slots. No goodbye: the Noise session that
